  "id": "COMPOUND:43279 - PROTEIN:4961",
  "verbalization": "Spirostan-3,27-diol, (3alpha)- is implicated in the biological activity of FaDu through a series of target relationships that converge on the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This subunit serves as a common target for multiple compounds, including Diplotrin A, Flavipin, and Pseudopterosin Q, all of which are linked to FaDu. The evidence suggests that Spirostan-3,27-diol, (3alpha)- may act as a modulator of the proteasome pathway, influencing the activity of these compounds and ultimately affecting FaDu. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Spirostan-3,27-diol, (3alpha)- could interact with FaDu, possibly through the regulation of proteasome function. The observed scores indicate a consistent and significant relationship, suggesting that the drug may exert its effects via a proteasome-dependent mechanism.",
